    "result_text": "Both tests pass. The full-stack change is complete and verified.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented project tracking as a small, additive full-stack change, mirroring the existing `clients` feature conventions:\n\n**Database** \u2014 `V3__projects.sql`: new `projects` table (`id`, `name`, `client_id` FK \u2192 `clients`), using `GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY` so the test seed can insert explicit fixture ids.\n\n**Server** (new `net.officefloor.hq.app.project` package):\n- `Project` entity + `ProjectRepository`\n- `NewProject` request body, `ProjectView` DTO (carries the joined client name)\n- `ListProjects` \u2014 `GET /api/projects`, joins `projects` to `clients` so each project surfaces the client's **name**, not id\n- `CreateProject` \u2014 `POST /api/projects`, validates name + client\n- New YAML endpoints `projects.GET.yml` / `projects.POST.yml` under `rest/api/`\n\n**Front-end** \u2014 new `features/projects/feature.tsx` (auto-discovered by the manifest router, giving `nav-projects`). It reads `/api/clients` to populate the client `<select>` (option values = client ids) and lists projects with `project-name` / `project-client`.\n\n**Test support** \u2014 extended `/__test__/seed` to insert `projects`, and `/__test__/reset` to truncate `projects` alongside `clients` (toggling H2 referential integrity so the FK-referenced tables truncate cleanly with identity restart).\n\nAll `data-testid` anchors match the spec exactly, and both `@core` tests pass. No pinned scaffolding or the test spec was touched.",
